IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `chr-dates`
IMPORT `chr-core`
IMPORT `chr-seat`

-- Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) -- worked cases for the injured person's questions
-- (chr-seat.l4), the rules (chr-core.l4) and the dates (chr-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the
-- deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated
-- facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative: a remand prisoner hurt in a privately run prison, a person held
-- in a police cell, a child in youth justice custody, a patient restrained and sedated in a locked ward.
-- Dates used: Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 commence 1 January 2008, Part 2 on 1 January 2007 (s 2); the 5th anniversary
-- of 10 May 2023 is 10 May 2028; of 29 February 2024 is 28 February 2029 (2029 has no 29 February: fork F9).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

-- kinds of body
`official` MEANS `a public official, such as a public servant, a department head or the staff of a public entity (Public Administration Act 2004)`
`statutory body` MEANS `a body set up by an Act or another statutory provision (for example a statutory authority, a public hospital or a school council)`
`police` MEANS `Victoria Police (a police officer or other member of Victoria Police)`
`council` MEANS `a council, a councillor or a member of council staff (Local Government Act 2020)`
`minister` MEANS `a Minister`
`committee` MEANS `members of a Parliamentary Committee`
`parliament` MEANS `Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament`
`tribunal` MEANS `a court or a tribunal`
`private body` MEANS `another body or person not set up by statute (for example a private company running a prison, a care provider or a contractor)`

-- s 4 answers
`PA official` MEANS `yes: a public official (s 4(1)(a))`
`PA statutory` MEANS `yes: an entity established by a statutory provision that has functions of a public nature (s 4(1)(b))`
`PA on behalf` MEANS `yes: an entity exercising functions of a public nature on behalf of the State or a public authority (s 4(1)(c))`
`PA police` MEANS `yes: Victoria Police (s 4(1)(d))`
`PA council` MEANS `yes: a Council, a Councillor or a member of Council staff (s 4(1)(e))`
`PA minister` MEANS `yes: a Minister (s 4(1)(f))`
`PA committee` MEANS `yes: members of a Parliamentary Committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(g))`
`PA declared` MEANS `yes: an entity declared by the regulations to be a public authority (s 4(1)(h))`
`PA court admin` MEANS `yes: a court or tribunal acting in an administrative capacity (not excluded by s 4(1)(j); a public authority under s 4(1)(b) when established by a statutory provision)`
`not PA parliament` MEANS `no: Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament, is not a public authority (s 4(1)(i))`
`not PA court` MEANS `no: a court or tribunal is not a public authority except when it is acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(j))`
`not PA declared` MEANS `no: an entity declared by the regulations not to be a public authority (s 4(1)(k))`
`not PA` MEANS `no: none of the kinds of public authority in s 4(1) (a)-(h)`

-- s 38 answers
`unlawful both` MEANS `yes: unlawful, both as an act incompatible with a human right and as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
`unlawful incompatible` MEANS `yes: unlawful as an act incompatible with a human right (s 38(1))`
`unlawful consideration` MEANS `yes: unlawful as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
`s38 not PA` MEANS `no: s 38 binds only public authorities, and this body is not one (s 4)`
`s38 too early` MEANS `no: Division 4 of Part 3 does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
`s38 private` MEANS `no: s 38 does not apply to an act or decision of a private nature (s 38(3))`
`s38 no choice` MEANS `no: s 38(1) does not apply, as the public authority could not reasonably have acted differently or made a different decision because of a statutory provision or other law (s 38(2))`
`s38 religious` MEANS `no: s 38(1) does not require the public authority to act in a way that impedes a religious body acting in conformity with its doctrines, beliefs or principles (s 38(4))`
`s38 not met` MEANS `no: on these facts the act was not incompatible with a human right, and any decision was made with proper consideration of the relevant human rights (s 38(1) not met)`

-- s 39 answers
`ground yes` MEANS `yes: I may seek the same relief or remedy on a ground of unlawfulness arising because of the Charter (s 39(1)), alongside my other claim`
`ground no claim` MEANS `no: the Charter gives no claim of its own; s 39(1) lets me add a Charter ground only to a claim I have apart from the Charter`
`ground too early` MEANS `no: s 39 is in Division 4 of Part 3, which does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
`ground not PA` MEANS `no: s 39(1) is about acts and decisions of a public authority, and this body is not one (s 4)`
`damages kept` MEANS `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); my right to damages under my other claim is not affected (s 39(4))`
`damages none` MEANS `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); and on my facts I have no other right to damages for the act`

-- s 32 answers
`read compatibly` MEANS `yes: so far as it is possible to do so consistently with its purpose, the provision must be interpreted compatibly with human rights (s 32(1)); if it cannot be, it stays valid (s 32(3)), and a declaration of inconsistent interpretation gives me no right or cause of action (s 36(5))`
`s32 not statutory` MEANS `no: s 32 applies to statutory provisions (Victorian Acts and subordinate instruments, s 3), and this law is not one`
`s32 override` MEANS `no: to the extent of an override declaration in force, the Charter has no application to the provision (s 31(6))`
`s32 old proceeding` MEANS `no: the Charter does not affect a proceeding commenced before 1 January 2007 (s 49(2))`
`s32 not yet` MEANS `no: s 32 was not in operation before 1 January 2008 (s 2(2))`
`Vic Act` MEANS `a Victorian Act`
`Vic instrument` MEANS `a Victorian subordinate instrument (regulations, rules or orders made under a Victorian Act)`
`Cth law` MEANS `a Commonwealth Act, or an instrument made under one`
`common law` MEANS `the common law (judge-made law, such as the law of negligence)`
`other place law` MEANS `the law of another State, a Territory or another country`

-- s 35 answers
`Supreme` MEANS `the Supreme Court`
`County` MEANS `the County Court`
`lower` MEANS `another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates' Court or VCAT)`
`notify both` MEANS `notice in the prescribed form to both the Attorney-General and the Commission (s 35(1))`
`notify Commission only` MEANS `notice in the prescribed form to the Commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 35(1), (2)(a))`
`notify AG only` MEANS `notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General only; none to the Commission, as it is a party (s 35(1), (2)(b))`
`notify none parties` MEANS `no notice: both the State and the Commission are parties (s 35(2))`
`notify none court` MEANS `no notice: s 35(1) requires one only for a Charter question in the Supreme Court or the County Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 33`
`given all` MEANS `yes: I have given every notice s 35 requires`
`none needed` MEANS `yes: s 35 requires no notice from me`
`still to give` MEANS `no: I have still to give a notice s 35 requires`

-- positions
`accused detained` MEANS `accused of an offence and detained`
`accused free` MEANS `accused of an offence and not detained`
`no charge` MEANS `detained without charge (for example by police, or under mental health or other law)`
`convicted` MEANS `convicted of an offence`
`no position` MEANS `none of these`

-- limbs
`L9 life` MEANS `s 9: the right to life`
`L9 deprived` MEANS `s 9: arbitrarily deprived of life`
`L10a` MEANS `s 10(a): subjected to torture`
`L10b` MEANS `s 10(b): treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way`
`L10c` MEANS `s 10(c): subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without full, free and informed consent`
`L13a` MEANS `s 13(a): privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with`
`L13b` MEANS `s 13(b): reputation unlawfully attacked`
`L21-1` MEANS `s 21(1): the right to liberty and security`
`L21-2` MEANS `s 21(2): arbitrary arrest or detention`
`L21-3` MEANS `s 21(3): deprived of liberty other than on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established by law`
`L21-4 reason` MEANS `s 21(4): not informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason for it`
`L21-4 proceedings` MEANS `s 21(4): not promptly informed about proceedings to be brought`
`L21-5a` MEANS `s 21(5)(a): not promptly brought before a court on a criminal charge`
`L21-5b` MEANS `s 21(5)(b): not brought to trial without unreasonable delay`
`L21-5c` MEANS `s 21(5)(c): not released when paragraph (a) or (b) was not complied with`
`L21-6` MEANS `s 21(6): automatically detained in custody while awaiting trial`
`L21-7 delay` MEANS `s 21(7): the court did not decide on the lawfulness of the detention without delay`
`L21-7 release` MEANS `s 21(7): the court did not order release after finding the detention unlawful`
`L21-8` MEANS `s 21(8): imprisoned only because of an inability to perform a contractual obligation`
`L22-1` MEANS `s 22(1): not treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person`
`L22-2` MEANS `s 22(2): an unconvicted detainee not segregated from convicted persons, where that was not reasonably necessary`
`L22-3` MEANS `s 22(3): an unconvicted detainee not treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted`
`L23-1` MEANS `s 23(1): a detained child not segregated from all detained adults`
`L23-2` MEANS `s 23(2): an accused child not brought to trial as quickly as possible`
`L23-3` MEANS `s 23(3): a convicted child not treated in a way appropriate for the child's age`
`L24-1` MEANS `s 24(1): the proceeding not decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing`
`L24-3` MEANS `s 24(3): the judgment or decision not made public`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`none` MEANS EMPTY

